+# 🌉 Bridge Work Order — [P1] Audit tracker: broken-in-production features consolidated — 10 findings, each with owning issue/PR, status and the single unblock action (bridge-20261027-audit-broken-tracker)
+
+## Problem
+The Bangla feature audit (2026-10-27) consolidated every production-breaking finding into one priority table. Each finding already owns an issue and (where applicable) a fix order or PR — 31 orders from this engagement alone. What does NOT exist is a single tracking point that answers, per broken feature: who owns it, what state it is in, and what is the one action that unblocks it.
+
+The cost of that absence is not theoretical: the guardian verdict-executor gap (#1331) was exactly this failure class — correct verdicts produced, nothing enacted, PRs rotted in the open. PR #334 (knowledge loop r2) is gate-green and waiting on an admin merge right now, with its predecessor #332 guardian-rejected (-13.5) but still open. Findings rot when their status lives only in session reports that the repo's own pipeline cannot see.
+
+This order is a **tracker, not a re-file**: it references existing issues; it files no duplicate fixes.
+
