+
+## Purpose and rules of this tracker
+1. One row, one owner, one unblock action — no prose. A row that cannot state its unblock action is itself a finding.
+2. This tracker never re-files a fix for a row; it updates status by comment and closes when rows 1–5 (all P0/P1) clear their unblock actions.
+3. When a row's owning PR merges, comment the merge run/PR number and strike the row.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+- [ ] Every row links to its owning issue(s) and states exactly one unblock action (verified above)
+- [ ] No new fix orders are filed from this tracker (reference-only discipline stated and honored)
+- [ ] Tracker is updated or closed once rows 1–5 clear their unblock actions
+- [ ] Repo operators can read the single table and know today's 2-minute decisions (merge #334, close #332)
+
+## Reflection Evidence (why + alternatives_rejected)
+**Why:** consolidation prevents gate-rot; the platform's own history in this audit (#1331 verdicts never enacted, #334 green-but-waiting) proves that findings without a live status surface decay silently. The bridge pipeline reads this repo, so the tracker becomes machine-visible state, not another local report.
+**Alternatives rejected:** (a) re-filing each broken feature as fresh orders — would duplicate 31 open orders and poison the dedupe discipline this pipeline depends on; (b) keeping the table only in the offline Bangla report — invisible to the repo's own autonomous builders, which is precisely the rot condition; (c) closing old issues and reopening consolidated ones — destroys evidence chains and in-flight PR references.
+
